      "id": 22,
      "url": "https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Kernel-install",
      "title": "ArchWiki kernel-install — plugin system, /etc/kernel/install.conf layout=bls|uki",
      "accessed": "2026-11-06",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "text": "kernel-install itself doesn't generate the initramfs, but utilizes plugins from programs like mkinitcpio or dracut instead.",
          "added": "2026-11-06"
        },
        {
          "text": "The main configuration file is /etc/kernel/install.conf. Use it to configure the layout you want to use, i.e. bls for traditional split kernel and initramfs images, or uki for Unified kernel images.",
          "added": "2026-11-06"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "url": "https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Mkinitcpio",
      "title": "ArchWiki Mkinitcpio — presets, MODULES/HOOKS/BINARIES/FILES, hook ordering + runtime functions",
      "accessed": "2026-11-06",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "text": "Hooks are small scripts describing what will be added to the initramfs image. Some hooks are accompanied by a so-called runtime hook providing startup functionality",
          "added": "2026-11-06"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 24,
      "url": "https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Pacman",
      "title": "ArchWiki Pacman — 5-step transaction plan, hooks, SigLevel, C + bsdtar",
      "accessed": "2026-11-06",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "text": "When successful, the workflow of a transaction follows five high-level steps plus pre/post transaction hooks:",
          "added": "2026-11-06"
        },
        {
          "text": "The default configuration, SigLevel = Required DatabaseOptional, enables signature verification for all the packages",
